# The uv-managed virtual environment, reconstructed by the recorded invocation
# from the checked-in `pyproject.toml` and `uv.lock`. uv also writes its own
# `.venv/.gitignore`, so this rule is redundant today; it is stated anyway
# because the alternative is that a several-hundred-megabyte tree stays out of
# diffs only through a tool's internal convention. The rule covers this one
# directory and nothing broader. Nothing else here is regenerable: the
# `record.tsv` under `results/` is the retained evidence and is tracked.
/.venv/
